  { "op": "held_by.remove", "position": "church-history-and-authority.fathers/valuable-but-subordinate", "tradition": "anglican",
    "reason": "Article 20 (Of the Authority of the Church) addresses the church's authority to decree rites and adjudicate controversies of faith; it never mentions the Fathers, patristic testimony, or their evidential weight. The Homilies portion of the citation could not be independently retrieved in this pass, so the entry is removed rather than kept on an unverified half." },

